# THE GAME's environment. Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your
# values - `dotenvy` resolves `.env` from the process WORKING DIRECTORY,
# which for the game is the deployment root (this directory).
#
# Split from the single combined `.env.example` on 2026-09-08, when the
# bot moved out of the workspace root into `bot/`. The bot's half is
# `bot/.env.example`; the two are disjoint, and no key appears in both.

# Which login holds the operator gates on the game's web dashboard:
# /admin/tunables, /admin/passives, the operator encounter trigger, the
# unfiltered /fights list, and the Operator tier on replay bundles. All
# five follow this one key, deliberately - a typo in one of several keys
# would leave the operator holding some surfaces and locked out of the
# rest. Compared case-insensitively; the value is lowercased on read.
#
# Leave unset for lokati_gaming, the value these gates were hardcoded to
# before this key existed. Changing it needs only a restart, not a
# rebuild. Point it at an account that EXISTS and has been logged into
# successfully before relying on it - loading /admin/tunables as that
# account is the check.
#
# Whatever this is set to is also refused at local registration, so a
# player can never claim the operator's name. `lokati_gaming` stays
# reserved regardless of this value.
OPERATOR_LOGIN=
